    "Publishing: network/ingest.ex, network/seed.ex and the techtree.network.seed mix task (ingest.ex names Techtree.Actors.Agent and RegentAgents.Authority, which this site has no counterpart for yet, so it cannot compile without a stand-in), the publication controller's create, limit_agent, received and record, publication_body.ex, publication_rate.ex, publication_address.ex, the endpoint's body reader and caps, and GET /api/v1/publication-keys/:key_id; they come with the publishing brief and its rulings.",
    "results_unreadable_error.ex: only Wallet Bench's evidence download raises it.",
    "The Results list's Wallet Bench tile (runs_live/index.ex): /wallet-bench is not on this site; it comes with the Wallet Bench brief.",
    "The Result page's share picture in the page head (runs_live/show.ex's share_image assign): this site's root document chooses each page's share picture by its path; ResultShareCard.image_url/1 and alt/1 wait for that.",
    "Techtree's Results telemetry event ([:techtree, :results, :read]), its rate limiting, visit log and Live.Session: this site's own apply.",
    "plugs/page_markdown.ex's :results, :result, :climb and :tdd answers, and the standing Results in controllers/sitemap_controller.ex: this site's one Markdown mechanism and sitemap are its own.",
    "priv/releases/ (the Climb release folders): nothing in Techtree's lib reads it.",
    "TechtreeWeb.GithubStars and its reader (the header's star count): they need a cache and a process kept running; the star link is shown without a count.",
    "The account menu (agents, Pair New Agent, Manage Account): this site's menu parts are not shared with products yet.",
    "The Blog (/blog): regents.sh has its own blog; whether Techtree's posts move is a later decision.",
    "priv/bootstrap/ (development.json, stable.json): no code reads it; Techtree's release documents name it.",
    "The techtree.bootstrap.list and techtree.bootstrap.publish mix tasks: the release commands cover the same two operations.",
    "The Docs' page_read plug and Techtree.Limits: this site's own limits apply, and pages are not counted.",
    "plugs/page_markdown.ex: the Docs answer Markdown through this site's RegentsWeb.PublicDocuments.document/1 instead.",
    "The rest of public_documents.ex (the /agents documents and page/1, formal/0, document?/1, trailer/0, llms/1, released_at/0, robots/0, security_txt/0, openapi/0, api_catalog/0, recovery_links/0, url/1), priv/public/openapi.json, Techtree.Capabilities and priv/tool_manifest.json: root documents are regents.sh's."
